Perfect! All tests are now passing. 

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`, which meant it was returning the second word instead of the first word. This caused the function to:
- Return 'world' instead of 'hello' for the input 'hello world'
- Crash with an IndexError for single-word inputs like 'solo'

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first element of the split list.
